INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5176,'https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1024604/openai-data-center-grid-protection-program','https://theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1024604/openai-data-center-grid-protection-program','OpenAI pitches data center power plants as a way to protect nearby areas','openaipitchesdatacenterpowerplantsasawaytoprotectnearbyareas','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-02T18:01:30Z','2026-11-03T04:04:57Z','In an announcement on Monday, OpenAI says it will pilot its "Grid Protectors Program" at an upcoming data center in Effingham County, Georgia, where the company promises to free up to 1,000 megawatts of power during extreme weather or emergencies, enough to power air conditioners in around 700,000 homes. The announcement comes as opposition to […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5177,'https://www.theverge.com/tech/1024588/brave-lawsuit-ai-scraping-new-york-times','https://theverge.com/tech/1024588/brave-lawsuit-ai-scraping-new-york-times','The New York Times sues Brave web browser for AI scraping and bypassing paywalls','thenewyorktimessuesbravewebbrowserforaiscrapingandbypassingpaywalls','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-02T17:51:19Z','2026-11-03T04:04:57Z','The New York Times and a group of other publications have filed lawsuits against the company that makes the Brave web browser over alleged unlawful scraping to train AI and also letting users bypass their paywalls, as reported by Reuters. According to a complaint filed by the New York Daily News, the Chicago Tribune, and […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5178,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/hkma-and-hkust-launch-pqc-toolkit-to-support-banks-quantum-preparedness/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/hkma-and-hkust-launch-pqc-toolkit-to-support-banks-quantum-preparedness','HKMA and HKUST Launch PQC Toolkit to Support Banks’ Quantum Preparedness','hkmaandhkustlaunchpqctoolkittosupportbanksquantumpreparedness','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-03T00:56:03Z','2026-11-03T04:04:57Z','HONG KONG, Nov. 2, 2026 — The Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) and The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) today launched the Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) Toolkit (Toolkit), with support from industry participants. The Toolkit sets out a structured and comprehensive framework to guide banks in planning and advancing their PQC transition journeys. […] The post HKMA and HKUST Launch PQC Toolkit to Support Banks’ Quantum Preparedness appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
