INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5690,'https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/11/04/ncsa-industry-conference-driving-innovation-with-ai-quantum-and-supercomputing/','https://hpcwire.com/2026/11/04/ncsa-industry-conference-driving-innovation-with-ai-quantum-and-supercomputing','NCSA Industry Conference: Driving Innovation with AI, Quantum, and Supercomputing','ncsaindustryconferencedrivinginnovationwithaiquantumandsupercomputing','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-05T01:36:56Z','2026-11-05T04:04:48Z','The National Center for Supercomputing Applications (NCSA) Industry Conference convenes researchers, technology providers and industry leaders who use advanced cyberinfrastructure (CI) to accelerate the process of discovery. All wrestle with the same challenges; how to apply the latest innovation for meaningful results without breaking the bank. NCSA was celebrating its 40th anniversary at the October […] The post NCSA Industry Conference: Driving Innovation with AI, Quantum, and Supercomputing appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5691,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/argonne-adds-ai-inference-capacity-for-genesis-mission-and-scientific-research/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/argonne-adds-ai-inference-capacity-for-genesis-mission-and-scientific-research','Argonne Adds AI Inference Capacity for Genesis Mission and Scientific Research','argonneaddsaiinferencecapacityforgenesismissionandscientificresearch','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-04T19:20:53Z','2026-11-05T04:04:48Z','New computing resources, including the powerful Tara system, are increasing the ALCF Inference Service’s capacity to support Genesis Mission projects and scientific research across the broader ALCF user community. Nov. 4, 2026 — The U.S. Department of Energy’s (DOE) Argonne National Laboratory is expanding the computing resources behind its Inference Service, giving researchers access to […] The post Argonne Adds AI Inference Capacity for Genesis Mission and Scientific Research appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5692,'https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/11/04/inside-a-turbulent-vortex-how-supercomputing-reveals-the-hidden-physics-of-flow/','https://hpcwire.com/2026/11/04/inside-a-turbulent-vortex-how-supercomputing-reveals-the-hidden-physics-of-flow','Inside a Turbulent Vortex: How Supercomputing Reveals the Hidden Physics of Flow','insideaturbulentvortexhowsupercomputingrevealsthehiddenphysicsofflow','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-04T18:38:08Z','2026-11-05T04:04:48Z','The Navier–Stokes equations have described the motion of fluids for nearly two centuries, yet they continue to pose some of the deepest challenges in mathematics and fluid mechanics. In September 2026, OpenAI announced a proposed solution to the long-standing existence and smoothness problem, showing how an initially smooth flow, driven by a smooth external force, […] The post Inside a Turbulent Vortex: How Supercomputing Reveals the Hidden Physics of Flow appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5693,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/cu-anschutz-researchers-evaluate-nih-effort-to-connect-research-data/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/cu-anschutz-researchers-evaluate-nih-effort-to-connect-research-data','CU Anschutz Researchers Evaluate NIH Effort to Connect Research Data','cuanschutzresearchersevaluatenihefforttoconnectresearchdata','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-04T18:12:54Z','2026-11-05T04:04:48Z','CU Anschutz researchers play a major role in evaluating research data from 18 programs to help scientists uncover relationships across studies and make better use of existing research. AURORA, Colo., Nov. 4, 2026 — Scientists generate vast amounts of research data, but connecting information across studies can be difficult. The NIH Common Fund Data Ecosystem […] The post CU Anschutz Researchers Evaluate NIH Effort to Connect Research Data appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(5694,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/universal-quantum-launches-iqpu-integrated-trapped-ion-processor/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/universal-quantum-launches-iqpu-integrated-trapped-ion-processor','Universal Quantum Launches iQPU Integrated Trapped-Ion Processor','universalquantumlaunchesiqpuintegratedtrappedionprocessor','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-04T17:21:45Z','2026-11-05T04:04:48Z','HAYWARDS HEATH, England and HAMBURG, Germany, Nov. 4, 2026 — Universal Quantum has launched the iQPU, an integrated quantum processing unit designed to make quantum computers practical to manufacture, scale and deploy cost effectively. Combining a massive trapped-ion compute surface with built-in ultra-low noise control technology and modular chip-to-chip interconnect (UQConnect) interfaces, the iQPU addresses some […] The post Universal Quantum Launches iQPU Integrated Trapped-Ion Processor appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
