INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6285,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/uchicago-receives-10m-grant-to-build-open-source-ai-weather-forecasting-platform/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/uchicago-receives-10m-grant-to-build-open-source-ai-weather-forecasting-platform','HPCwire - Since 1987','hpcwire','websearch_en','hpcwire.com','en','2026-11-07T04:03:35Z','2026-11-07T04:03:41Z','UChicago''s Human-Centered Weather Forecasts initiative sent AI forecasts by text message to tens of millions of farmers in Africa and South Asia from 2024 to 2026. Those forecasts correctly predicted an unusual stall in seasonal rains, providing an early warning to farmers.',4.0,'classified',NULL,56);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6286,'https://www.sixthtone.com/news/1019225','https://sixthtone.com/news/1019225','China’s Sea Goddess Has a New Job: AI Weather Forecasting','chinasseagoddesshasanewjobaiweatherforecasting','websearch_en','sixthtone.com','en','2026-11-07T04:03:35Z','2026-11-07T04:03:41Z','China handed over equipment for a customized MAZU AI weather prediction tool to Sri Lanka, where it will form part of a system to warn of heavy rain, strong winds, and cyclones, expected to enter service by the end of the year. In Djibouti, the model helps provide tailored weather warnings for the port.',5.0,'classified',NULL,54);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6287,'https://www.noaa.gov/news/noaa-voices-at-2026-oral-history-association-annual-meeting-ext','https://noaa.gov/news/noaa-voices-at-2026-oral-history-association-annual-meeting-ext','NOAA Voices at the 2026 Oral History Association Annual Meeting','noaavoicesatthe2026oralhistoryassociationannualmeeting','noaa_news','NOAA news','en','2026-11-06T11:59:56Z','2026-11-07T04:03:42Z','NOAA Voices at the 2026 Oral History Association Annual Meeting The 60th Annual Oral History Association Meeting will take place October 14–17, 2026, in Portland, Oregon. This year’s theme, “Landscapes of Memory,” explores relationships among place, memory, movement, and changing environmental, political, and cultural landscapes. NOAA Voices Oral Historian and Archivist Molly Graham is serving as a program co-chair, and many NOAA Voices project partners will be among the presenters and attendees. Registration is now open. Learn more, view the program, and register at the OHA Annual Meeting web',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6288,'https://www.noaa.gov/news/project-jukebox-ext','https://noaa.gov/news/project-jukebox-ext','University of Alaska Fairbanks Oral History Program''s Project Jukebox','universityofalaskafairbanksoralhistoryprogramsprojectjukebox','noaa_news','NOAA news','en','2026-11-06T11:54:13Z','2026-11-07T04:03:42Z','University of Alaska Fairbanks Oral History Program''s Project Jukebox We are excited to partner with the University of Alaska Fairbanks Oral History Program''s Project Jukebox to co-locate selected oral histories, expanding access to one of the nation''s most innovative digital oral history collections, where interviews are integrated with photographs, maps, and place-based storytelling to document Alaska''s diverse communities, cultures, and changing environments. Download Image EXT link test 0 Off',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6289,'https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/about-us/news-and-media/media-centre/weather-and-climate-news/2026/strong-el-nino-drives-2027-co-rise-towards-record-levels','https://metoffice.gov.uk/about-us/news-and-media/media-centre/weather-and-climate-news/2026/strong-el-nino-drives-2027-co-rise-towards-record-levels','Strong El Niño drives 2027 CO₂ rise towards record levels The Met Office forecasts an unusually large rise in atmospheric carbon dioxide (CO₂) for 2027, diverging further from 1.5°C-compatible pathways as strong El Niño amplifies the human-driven rise by weakening natural carbon sinks. Read more','strongelninodrives2027co2risetowardsrecordlevelsthemetofficeforecastsanunusuallylargeriseinatmosphericcarbondioxideco2for2027divergingfurtherfrom15ccompatiblepathwaysasstrongelninoamplifiesthehumandrivenrisebyweakeningnaturalcarbonsinksreadmore','metoffice_news','UK Met Office news','en',NULL,'2026-11-07T04:03:42Z','',2.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6290,'https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/telco-open-source-tools-research-6g-networks/','https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/telco-open-source-tools-research-6g-networks','How NVIDIA Open Source Tools Are Helping Researchers Build Next-Generation 6G Networks','hownvidiaopensourcetoolsarehelpingresearchersbuildnextgeneration6gnetworks','nvidia_blog','NVIDIA blog','en','2026-11-06T16:00:35Z','2026-11-07T04:03:43Z','A year ago, NVIDIA open sourced its Aerial wireless software, joining Sionna and a broader suite of open source tools for accelerating next-generation 6G network development. Together, they give researchers a foundation for testing ideas, comparing results and building on each other’s work — connecting simulation and AI training with experiments on real over-the-air wireless […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6291,'https://eos.org/editors-vox/announcing-the-new-agu-publications-editors-in-chief-starting-in-2027','https://eos.org/editors-vox/announcing-the-new-agu-publications-editors-in-chief-starting-in-2027','Announcing the New AGU Publications Editors-in-Chief Starting in 2027','announcingthenewagupublicationseditorsinchiefstartingin2027','eos','Eos (AGU)','en','2026-11-06T14:52:56Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Credit: aheflin, Adobe Stock',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6292,'https://eos.org/articles/deep-diving-rocks-reveal-a-subduction-zones-thermal-secrets','https://eos.org/articles/deep-diving-rocks-reveal-a-subduction-zones-thermal-secrets','Deep-Diving Rocks Reveal a Subduction Zone’s Thermal Secrets','deepdivingrocksrevealasubductionzonesthermalsecrets','eos','Eos (AGU)','en','2026-11-06T14:11:35Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Rocks collected from Goodenough Island, Papua New Guinea, shown here, are revealing the physical conditions of subduction zones. Credit: Paul Fitzgerald',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6293,'https://eos.org/research-spotlights/what-triggered-an-ancient-magma-surge-in-the-north-cascades','https://eos.org/research-spotlights/what-triggered-an-ancient-magma-surge-in-the-north-cascades','What Triggered an Ancient Magma Surge in the North Cascades?','whattriggeredanancientmagmasurgeinthenorthcascades','eos','Eos (AGU)','en','2026-11-06T14:10:58Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Advancements in high-precision rock dating are helping to clarify the complex geologic history of the North Cascades in Washington. Credit: Sourav Karmakar',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6294,'https://eos.org/thelandslideblog/the-25-26-september-2026-cluster-of-landslides-in-tanintharyi-region-myanmar','https://eos.org/thelandslideblog/the-25-26-september-2026-cluster-of-landslides-in-tanintharyi-region-myanmar','The 25-26 September 2026 cluster of landslides in Tanintharyi Region, Myanmar','the2526september2026clusteroflandslidesintanintharyiregionmyanmar','eos','Eos (AGU)','en','2026-11-06T07:59:33Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Planet Labs image showing the landslides triggered by the 25-26 September 2026 rainstorm in Myanmar. Image copyright Planet Labs, used with permission.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6295,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-method-microplastics-air-uncrewed-aerial.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-method-microplastics-air-uncrewed-aerial.html','New method measures microplastics in the air using an uncrewed aerial system','newmethodmeasuresmicroplasticsintheairusinganuncrewedaerialsystem','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T21:20:04Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Microplastics have been found in our bodies and the food we eat—and even in remote environments around the world, including seawater and ice in the Arctic. Despite their prevalence, little is known about how they move through the atmosphere. New CIRES-led research, which demonstrates a new method for sampling microplastics in the atmosphere using an uncrewed aerial system (UAS), aims to change that. The findings are published in the journal Scientific Reports.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6296,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-future-events-outdo-extreme.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-future-events-outdo-extreme.html','Future warming events will outdo the extreme heat waves of the recent past, new study finds','futurewarmingeventswilloutdotheextremeheatwavesoftherecentpastnewstudyfinds','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T21:00:01Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','The extreme heat waves we have seen over the last few years may only serve as a preview of what is to come as a result of climate change. A new study led by researcher Philipp Aglas-Leitner from Freie Universität Berlin, published in Nature Communications, finds that future heat waves could last longer, impact larger areas, and be much more severe.',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6297,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-european-forests-crises-necessarily.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-european-forests-crises-necessarily.html','European forests need to solve two crises—but not necessarily in one place','europeanforestsneedtosolvetwocrisesbutnotnecessarilyinoneplace','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T20:00:01Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Forest areas can act both as carbon sinks and as vital habitats for thousands of species—but not necessarily at the same time. This has important implications for how Europe should manage its forests, says a University of Copenhagen researcher.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6298,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mtg-i2-satellite-remarkable-images.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mtg-i2-satellite-remarkable-images.html','MTG-I2 satellite delivers remarkable first images, capturing a weather view of Europe every 2.5 minutes','mtgi2satellitedeliversremarkablefirstimagescapturingaweatherviewofeuropeevery25minutes','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T19:40:10Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Europe''s meteorological satellite agency, EUMETSAT, has released the first image from the Flexible Combined Imager (FCI) on board Meteosat Third Generation Imager 2 (MTG-I2), just over two months after the satellite''s launch on Aug. 27, 2026. The satellite will provide forecasters with high-resolution observations of Europe every 2.5 minutes. This unprecedented frequency will help forecasters monitor fast-developing weather hazards more closely and support earlier, more precise warnings.',4.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6299,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-high-precision-timeline-ancient-magma.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-high-precision-timeline-ancient-magma.html','High-precision timeline helps clarify an ancient magma surge in the North Cascades','highprecisiontimelinehelpsclarifyanancientmagmasurgeinthenorthcascades','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T19:40:06Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Where oceanic crust subducts beneath continental crust, belts of volcanoes known as continental arcs can form. Located around the world, these arcs may undergo episodic magma flare-ups—dramatic surges in the flow of magma into the continental crust at rates up to 20 times higher than normal. However, what triggers these extreme surges, which last tens of millions of years, can be unclear.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6300,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mega-interaction-soil-moisture-atmospheric.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mega-interaction-soil-moisture-atmospheric.html','''Mega heat waves'' strengthened by interaction between soil moisture, atmospheric pressure and temperature','megaheatwavesstrengthenedbyinteractionbetweensoilmoistureatmosphericpressureandtemperature','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T19:00:08Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','A new study has found that a self-reinforcing interaction between temperature, soil moisture and atmospheric pressure is being triggered at high temperatures, making extreme heat waves 10% hotter than they would otherwise be. The study was published in Science Advances and led by the Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research (PIK) and the International Institute for Applied Systems Analysis (IIASA).',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6301,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-worse-climate-harder.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-worse-climate-harder.html','The worse climate change gets, the harder it becomes to stop it','theworseclimatechangegetstheharderitbecomestostopit','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T18:20:01Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','This year may be seen as a turning point in the climate crisis. The U.N. has accepted that global warming is going to exceed 1.5°C, while climate scientists have concluded that the rate of warming has effectively doubled over the past decade.',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6302,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-foreign-investment-african.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-foreign-investment-african.html','How foreign investment can strengthen African governments'' control over land','howforeigninvestmentcanstrengthenafricangovernmentscontroloverland','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T15:30:01Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','African governments are using foreign investment, infrastructure projects and conservation schemes to extend their control over land and communities, according to new research spanning 14 countries in sub-Saharan Africa.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6303,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-microplastic-pollution-pacific-ocean.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-microplastic-pollution-pacific-ocean.html','Microplastic pollution could be changing the color of the Pacific Ocean','microplasticpollutioncouldbechangingthecolorofthepacificocean','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T15:20:01Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Our oceans have effectively become trash dumps where massive quantities of plastic end up. So much so, in fact, that the largest offshore plastic accumulation zone has been labeled the Great Pacific Garbage Patch.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6304,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mineral-method-radioactive-technetium-liquid.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-mineral-method-radioactive-technetium-liquid.html','Mineral-forming method removes more than 99% of radioactive technetium from liquid waste','mineralformingmethodremovesmorethan99ofradioactivetechnetiumfromliquidwaste','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T15:00:05Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','Technetium-99 is a long-lived radioactive byproduct of nuclear fuel production and reprocessing. In many environments, it forms a highly mobile chemical species that can move readily through water and soil, making it a priority contaminant at legacy nuclear sites including Sellafield in the U.K. and Hanford in the United States.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6305,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-hottest-year-eu.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-hottest-year-eu.html','2026 ''most likely'' to be second-hottest year on record: EU monitor','2026mostlikelytobesecondhottestyearonrecordeumonitor','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T13:00:09Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','The world is on track for 2026 to be the second-hottest year on record as an exceptionally strong El Niño weather pattern turbocharges human-driven global warming, the EU''s climate monitor said Friday.',2.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6306,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-forests-underground-storage-metric-carbon.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-forests-underground-storage-metric-carbon.html','Forests or underground storage? New metric compares risks of carbon removal projects','forestsorundergroundstoragenewmetriccomparesrisksofcarbonremovalprojects','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T10:00:13Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','The risk of relying on uncertain carbon removal projects can now be quantified using a new standardized metric that can be applied across all such schemes, irrespective of the technology used.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6307,'https://phys.org/news/2026-11-high-elevation-terraces-faster-uplift.html','https://phys.org/news/2026-11-high-elevation-terraces-faster-uplift.html','High-elevation terraces suggest faster-than-expected uplift in southern Italy','highelevationterracessuggestfasterthanexpectedupliftinsouthernitaly','phys_earth','Phys.org Earth news','en','2026-11-06T10:00:08Z','2026-11-07T04:03:44Z','University of Oregon geologist Becky Dorsey''s latest research sheds light on the Siculo-Calabrian rift zone, a belt of faults spanning more than 100 miles (160 kilometers) in southern Italy. The new data could help improve earthquake hazard assessment in this seismically active region.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6308,'https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1029380/openai-1-25-trillion-investment-valuation','https://theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1029380/openai-1-25-trillion-investment-valuation','OpenAI valued at $1.25 trillion, as rival Anthropic nears its IPO','openaivaluedat125trillionasrivalanthropicnearsitsipo','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-06T23:46:18Z','2026-11-07T04:03:45Z','OpenAI is now valued at $1.25 trillion in a new round of funding that has raised another $11 billion, according to Bloomberg. That would make it one of the world''s most valuable companies, not long after raising $122 billion from investors in March at a valuation of $852 billion. Echoing FT and Wall Street Journal […]',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6309,'https://www.theverge.com/tech/1029338/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-china-spy','https://theverge.com/tech/1029338/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-china-spy','China reportedly recruited AI exec to spy on Jensen Huang','chinareportedlyrecruitedaiexectospyonjensenhuang','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-06T23:00:44Z','2026-11-07T04:03:45Z','China''s intelligence agency recruited Megaspeed executive Alice Huang to spy on Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, according to The New York Times. The Ministry of State Security (MSS) enlisted her to glean information about American AI chips and "potentially influence the company to push for its most advanced chips to be made available to China." Megaspeed […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6310,'https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/902546/data-centers-ai-energy-power-grids-controversy','https://theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/902546/data-centers-ai-energy-power-grids-controversy','All the latest updates on AI data centers','allthelatestupdatesonaidatacenters','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-06T20:02:22Z','2026-11-07T04:03:45Z','Massive new data centers are the physical foundation for tech companies’ hopes and dreams for AI. But the rush to expand warehouses full of energy-hungry servers has also kicked up fights across the world over their impact on power grids, utility bills, nearby communities, and the environment. Data centers were a major bipartisan issue ahead […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6311,'https://www.theverge.com/tech/1028871/meta-muse-ai-spaces','https://theverge.com/tech/1028871/meta-muse-ai-spaces','Meta’s Muse AI can create custom ‘spaces’ for the version of the app you need right now','metasmuseaicancreatecustomspacesfortheversionoftheappyouneedrightnow','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-06T18:10:10Z','2026-11-07T04:03:45Z','Meta will now allow you to build customized, app-like experiences within Muse. The new feature, called "spaces," allows its AI assistant to build things like a shopping hub, school dashboard, music tracker, trivia game, and more, which you can interact with directly in the Muse app. Meta says you can create a new space by […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6312,'https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1028609/ai-dating-feelings-doomers-singularity','https://theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1028609/ai-dating-feelings-doomers-singularity','AI is the new dating dealbreaker','aiisthenewdatingdealbreaker','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-11-06T17:00:00Z','2026-11-07T04:03:45Z','When Irene moved to San Francisco last year, she started using dating apps as a way to meet new people, get to know her new city, and connect with others who care about the things she does. After the 25-year-old analyst downloaded Hinge and started swiping, she noticed a trend. "Hinge has a prompt where […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
