INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6912,'https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/11/09/ai-and-medicine-data-availability-transparency-and-trust-and-validation/','https://hpcwire.com/2026/11/09/ai-and-medicine-data-availability-transparency-and-trust-and-validation','AI and Medicine: Data Availability, Transparency and Trust, and Validation','aiandmedicinedataavailabilitytransparencyandtrustandvalidation','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-09T19:09:25Z','2026-11-10T04:04:59Z','Editor’s note: HPCwire contributor Steve Conway conducted a three-part interview with Frederick H. Hausheer, MD and Fellow of the American College of Physicians (FACP), a medical oncologist and clinical pharmacologist who heads Hausheer BioMed, an oncology and pharmaceutical-industry research and development consulting firm. Part 1 of the series, “AI and Medicine: Who’s the Doctor?,” ran on […] The post AI and Medicine: Data Availability, Transparency and Trust, and Validation appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6913,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/q-ant-and-ionos-launch-photonic-computing-pilot/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/q-ant-and-ionos-launch-photonic-computing-pilot','Q.ANT and IONOS Launch Photonic Computing Pilot','qantandionoslaunchphotoniccomputingpilot','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-09T19:03:55Z','2026-11-10T04:04:59Z','IONOS bare metal servers provide the foundation for companies, researchers, and developers to run AI models on Q.ANT’s photonic hardware. STUTTGART, Germany and KARLSRUHE, Germany, Nov. 9, 2026 — Q.ANT, a pioneer in commercial photonic computing, today announced the launch of a joint pilot program with IONOS, the leading digitalization partner and trusted cloud enabler […] The post Q.ANT and IONOS Launch Photonic Computing Pilot appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(6914,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/cerabyte-to-address-future-of-data-storage-for-hpc-and-ai-at-sc26/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/cerabyte-to-address-future-of-data-storage-for-hpc-and-ai-at-sc26','Cerabyte to Address Future of Data Storage for HPC and AI at SC26','cerabytetoaddressfutureofdatastorageforhpcandaiatsc26','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-11-09T18:54:39Z','2026-11-10T04:04:59Z','Cerabyte Joins Los Alamos National Laboratory to Discuss Storage Innovation SANTA CLARA, Calif. and CHICAGO, Nov. 9, 2026 — Cerabyte today announced that it will join experts from Los Alamos National Laboratory for a panel discussion at Supercomputing 2026 (SC26). The experts will examine how industry consolidation, limited investment in long-cycle research/development and growing AI […] The post Cerabyte to Address Future of Data Storage for HPC and AI at SC26 appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
